---
description: Keep each backend method to a single job
alwaysApply: true
---

# Backend method responsibility

When adding or changing C# in `api/` or `worker/`, each method does one job.
Do this in the same change as the method.

- A method that validates, loads, calculates, and saves in one body is too
  big. Call one method for each of those jobs.
- A pure calculation goes in `Domain`. See
  `.cursor/rules/backend-domain-rules.mdc`.
- Loading and saving stay in `Services`.
- Assigning the fields for one write can stay in that write method.
- Do not add these splits to generated EF Core migration files.

```csharp
public async Task<AccountDto> ReconcileAsync(...)
{
    var account = await FindAccountAsync(...);
    RequireOpenAccount(account);
    var adjustment = await CalculateAdjustmentAsync(...);
    await SaveAdjustmentAsync(account, adjustment);
    return await ProjectAccountAsync(account.Id);
}
```
